# Copy to .env and adjust. SQLite keeps the zero-config local story:
#   bun run db:push && bun run db:seed
# The path is resolved relative to prisma/schema.prisma.

# ---- Database -------------------------------------------------------------
# SQLite by default (zero-config local dev). The `db/` folder lives at the
# repo root, git-ignored. A RELATIVE `file:` URL is resolved against
# prisma/schema.prisma — exactly like the Prisma CLI — so `file:../db/custom.db`
# points at <repo>/db/custom.db for the CLI (migrate/seed), `next build`, and
# the running server alike, regardless of the process working directory.
# (src/lib/db-path.ts implements this resolution; tests/db-path.test.ts
# pins the contract.)
# For production, an ABSOLUTE path is still recommended — see
# docs/DEPLOYMENT.md §4.
# To use PostgreSQL:
#   1. Set provider = "postgresql" in prisma/schema.prisma
#   2. Set DATABASE_URL to a PostgreSQL connection string
#   3. bun run db:push && bun run db:seed
DATABASE_URL="file:../db/custom.db"
# PostgreSQL example:
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/digma

# Optional escape hatch when neither the CWD nor the module path can find
# the repo (e.g. a container that copied the standalone output + prisma/ to
# /app): an explicit repo root for db-path.ts anchor resolution.
# DIGMA_REPO_ROOT=/app

# ---- Auth -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Session signing secret for HMAC cookie auth (src/lib/auth.ts reads
# AUTH_SECRET). REQUIRED in production: generate with `openssl rand -hex 32`.
# Falls back to an insecure dev-only constant when unset.
AUTH_SECRET=""

# ---- Auth delivery --------------------------------------------------------
# Optional production knob (session 64, S64-D): set to "1" to suppress the
# SELF-HOSTED in-app password-reset link — the forgot-password route stops
# returning `resetUrl` in its response (the no-enumeration 200 and its
# message are unchanged; the login card's "Check your email" state simply
# renders without the demo link). Set this when a real email service owns
# the reset delivery: the live single-use token never rides an API payload.
# (The OTP verification code's in-response delivery is the same ADR-014
# self-hosted family — the register/resend routes keep it for the demo
# verify flow.)
# DIGMA_DISABLE_IN_APP_RESET=1

# Optional production knob (session 67, S67-C): the OTP half of the same
# ADR-014 suppression family. Set to "1" and the three verification-code
# delivery sites (register's response, login's unverified-branch response,
# and resend-otp's response) answer with `verificationCode: null` — the
# 6-digit code goes NOWHERE until a real email service owns the delivery.
# Set BOTH knobs for the closed production posture: no credential (reset
# token or verify code) ever rides an API payload.
# DIGMA_DISABLE_IN_APP_OTP=1

# ---- Rate limiting / proxy topology ---------------------------------------
# Optional production knob (session 69, S69-A): the DECLARED number of
# trusted appending proxies in front of the app — how the per-IP rate
# limiter (src/lib/rate-limit.ts) derives a client key from
# x-forwarded-for. Unset (the default) = 1, the "exactly one appending
# proxy" trust: the limiter keys on the LAST hop, which that proxy
# appended — correct behind one reverse proxy (nginx/Caddy forwarding
# X-Forwarded-For), and the form every test suite uses.
#   0    = DIRECT EXPOSURE (no proxy): x-forwarded-for and x-real-ip are
#          IGNORED entirely — every caller keys one shared bucket. Honest
#          self-throttling instead of the bypassable alternative (a client
#          rotating XFF per request would otherwise key a fresh bucket on
#          every call and the 10/15-min auth + 20/5-min assistant limits
#          would never trip). Prefer deploying behind a proxy at depth 1.
#   N>=2 = N appending proxies: the limiter keys on the hop the Nth proxy
#          preserved (the client IP), NOT the last hop — which at two or
#          more hops is the innermost PROXY's own IP and would collapse
#          every user into one self-DoS bucket. A header with fewer hops
#          than declared fails closed onto the shared bucket.
# An unparsable or negative value fails closed onto the default (1).
# DIGMA_PROXY_HOPS=1

# ---- AI assistant ---------------------------------------------------------
# Optional force-degrade knob: set to "1" to skip the z-ai-web-dev-sdk LLM
# path entirely and answer every assistant command from the deterministic
# fallback parser (src/lib/ai-assistant.ts). The Playwright e2e webServer
# sets this so the suite pins the fallback's exact replies (the SDK is
# reachable from the standalone server and its free-form replies are
# non-deterministic); production can use it to force the degrade path.
# DIGMA_DISABLE_AI_LLM=1

# ---- SEO surfaces --------------------------------------------------------
# Session 99 (S99-G — the SEO parity): the PUBLIC ORIGIN the SEO surfaces
# declare — /robots.txt's sitemap pointer and /sitemap.xml's absolute URLs
# (src/app/robots.ts + src/app/sitemap.ts, the Next Metadata-route
# conventions; the reference app serves both — measured live at the 75th
# reference audit). Unset = http://localhost:3000 (the local default).
# Set it to your deployed origin (no trailing slash) when you serve the
# app publicly, e.g.:
# DIGMA_SITE_URL=https://digma.example.com

# ---- Test infrastructure (read by the Playwright layer, not the app) ----
# Session 85 (S85-E / B85-I1): the honest attribution — the Playwright CONFIG
# reads E2E_PORT; E2E_BASE_URL is read by the seven spec files that build
# their own request contexts (export-png, mobile-properties, session58/60/
# 61-fixes, session85-fixes, and auth — session 102's S102-D added auth's
# from_url guard to the family, deriving its expected origin from the
# knob instead of a hardcoded port). The app itself never reads either.
# Session 86 (S86-C / B86-L1): the count is LIVE-DERIVED — tests/
# doc-lows-s86.test.ts greps the spec files and asserts this header's
# number equals the grep count (the S85-E header said "five" while
# session85-fixes — a reader — landed in the same commit; the honesty
# fix undercounted its own delivery).
# E2E_PORT=3100
# E2E_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3100
